==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|gem-pro|skakanan|lang=ang}}. Cognate with Old Saxon [[skakan]], Old Norse [[skaka]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈʃɑkɑn/|lang=ang}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb|type=strong|class=VI}}

# {{intransitive}} to [[pass]] or [[depart]]
# {{intransitive}} to [[quiver]] or [[vibrate]]
# {{transitive}} to [[flourish]] or [[wave]] (an object)
# {{transitive}} to cause something to [[quiver]], [[flutter]], or [[shake]]

====Descendants====
* English: to [[shake]]